WEBVTT

english-organize-revise-clear-paragraph-narration-caption-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.085
Show me: I will not rewrite your paragraph. First, underline the sentence that states your point so we can see the path your details should follow.

english-organize-revise-clear-paragraph-narration-caption-2
00:00:08.085 --> 00:00:17.655
Talk me through it: tell me what you want the reader to understand first. Then we will test one sentence at a time against that point, and you will choose the final revision.

english-organize-revise-clear-paragraph-narration-caption-3
00:00:17.655 --> 00:00:25.080
Let’s do one together. A paragraph begins with two examples and states its main point last. What is the smallest useful first revision?

english-organize-revise-clear-paragraph-narration-caption-4
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:34.210
Different example: if a draft gives a detail, then a closing, then its point, try moving the existing point first. Keep the wording that still sounds like the writer.
